{
	"$comment": [
		"Subject tags for the magisterial documents, `document slug -> [tag, ...]`, merged into the",
		"shipped index by scripts/sync-corpus.mjs and read by /documenta's filter panel.",
		"",
		"WHY THIS FILE EXISTS RATHER THAN A FIELD IN the corpus's build/*/manifest.json: exactly the",
		"reason descriptions.json gives. Those manifests are GENERATED, a re-parse rewrites them, and",
		"this project fixes parsers by re-parsing. A tag is editorial -- it is what someone concluded",
		"the document is ABOUT, which no scraper can read off a page -- so it lives in tracked source",
		"here and is merged in on the way to the site.",
		"",
		"KEYED BY DOCUMENT SLUG, NOT BY WORK ID, and that is the difference from descriptions.json.",
		"A description is prose about the text that was READ, so it belongs to one edition; a tag is",
		"about the document, and every edition of Rerum Novarum is about labour. Same key the",
		"translated-descriptions files use, and the same key /documenta/{slug} addresses.",
		"",
		"THE VOCABULARY IS CLOSED. `vocabulary` below is the whole of it and `sync-corpus.mjs` exits 1",
		"on a tag outside it. It was OPEN and 232 terms wide for one day (2026-08-31) and the two ends",
		"of that distribution were each useless in their own way, which is why it was cut to 53:",
		"  - THE TAIL was 46 terms on one document apiece and 50 more on two -- `dueling`, `Dante`,",
		"    `Amazon`, `Fatima`. A facet row that narrows 272 documents to one is a worse way of",
		"    reaching that document than its title, and it made the panel unreadable at the size where",
		"    the useful terms live.",
		"  - THE HEAD held terms that did not partition anything: `centenary` (35) and `anniversary`",
		"    say what OCCASIONED a document, not what it treats; `Vatican II` (23) and `synod` (22)",
		"    restate the author and kind facets sitting above them; `saints` survived because",
		"    commemorating a saint IS a subject, while the occasion words around it are not.",
		"  - 35 REGION NAMES went too, and they were the closest call. `Mexico` and `Hungary` are real",
		"    subjects and a reader does want them. They are dropped from the FACET and not from the",
		"    site: every one of them is in the document's description, which the search box now reads.",
		"",
		"A SECOND HEAD CUT, 2026-08-31, took `errors condemned` (37) out for the reason `centenary`",
		"went: it names what a document DOES and not what it is about. Nearly every magisterial text",
		"rejects something, so the term had attached itself to `spe-salvi`, `mysterium`,",
		"`providentissimus-deus` and `fratelli-tutti` alongside `pascendi` -- and its co-occurrence was",
		"flat across the whole vocabulary (nothing above 8, spread over theology, saints, family,",
		"Christology, social doctrine), which is the signature of a rhetorical mode rather than a",
		"subject. The documents that really are anti-error keep the error they name: `Freemasonry`,",
		"`communism`, `socialism`, `philosophy`, `Thomism`, `Christian unity`. `Church and State` (42)",
		"was weighed in the same pass and KEPT: its 42 are one question -- the Church before civil",
		"power, from `vehementer-nos` and `mit-brennender-sorge` to `dignitatis-humanae` -- and its",
		"co-occurrence is concentrated where that question goes (`persecution` 13, `religious liberty`",
		"3 of 6, `education` 10), so the size is the subject being that large. Since subjects now",
		"SUBTRACT, a broad term is the best first click and not a dead end: it meets `education` at 10",
		"documents and `marriage` at 5.",
		"",
		"NAMED ERRORS REPLACED THE MODE TERM, same day. `errors condemned` was dropped for saying what",
		"a document DOES; what it was standing in for is the error each document actually treats, and",
		"that IS a subject. `communism`, `socialism` and `Freemasonry` were already here in that shape,",
		"so five more were derived from the English descriptions and then READ, never counted:",
		"`rationalism` (6), `naturalism` (5), `modernism` (4), `atheism` (4), `materialism` (3). They",
		"fill a real hole -- `pascendi-dominici-gregis` carried philosophy, seminaries, Scripture and",
		"Thomism and nothing naming Modernism, which is the whole of it -- and they barely overlap: 22",
		"assignments over 17 documents, largest pairwise intersection 2, so they are not five words for",
		"one thing.",
		"",
		"WHAT DID NOT CLEAR THE BAR IS THE MORE USEFUL HALF OF THAT SCAN. The ANCIENT heresies are not",
		"subjects in this corpus and no vocabulary will make them so: Arianism, Americanism, Jansenism,",
		"Gallicanism, Manichaeism, Donatism, pantheism, positivism and immanentism appear in ZERO",
		"descriptions, and Pelagianism, Nestorianism and Monophysitism in one or two apiece -- always",
		"inside a document commemorating the Father who fought them (`aeterna-dei`,",
		"`orientalis-ecclesiae`, `ad-salutem-humani`), where the subject is the saint and `saints`",
		"already holds it. The corpus runs Leo XIII to Francis; the errors it is about are that",
		"period's.",
		"",
		"TWO NEAR-MISSES WORTH NOT REPEATING. `gnosticism` scored 3 and is 1: the other two hits were",
		"the string `agnosticism` inside `pascendi` and `communium-rerum`. And `secularism` scored 5",
		"and is 2 -- `tametsi-futura-prospicientibus` lists it as a consequence, `grata-recordatio` as",
		"a prayer intention, `sancta-dei-civitas` as background to a missions letter. It stays out on a",
		"second ground too: the documents that would carry it are the separation-law encyclicals, which",
		"`Church and State` and `persecution` already hold. Counting a word proposes a candidate;",
		"reading the sentence is what decides it.",
		"",
		"THAT SEARCH BOX IS WHY THE CUT IS SAFE. `/documenta` searches title, author, kind, description",
		"and tags together, so a term worth finding does not need a facet row to be findable. Read the",
		"facet as the small set of axes worth BROWSING by, and the search as everything else.",
		"",
		"Adding a term to `vocabulary` is a deliberate act: it costs a row in every reader's panel, so",
		"it should name an axis someone would browse, and should already fit several documents. Prefer",
		"an existing term -- a synonym splits a term's documents in two and neither half is findable.",
		"Casing is meaning (proper nouns capitalised, common nouns not) and the sync refuses two terms",
		"differing only in case, since the panel matches case-insensitively.",
		"",
		"THE TERMS ARE NOT TRANSLATED and render verbatim; only the panel around them is. A closed list",
		"could in principle carry an i18n key each, the way `document_kind` does in document-labels.ts,",
		"but 53 terms is 742 strings across the fourteen dictionaries and nobody has asked for them.",
		"",
		"HOW THESE WERE DERIVED, because a tag is a judgement and its basis should be on the record.",
		"Each was written by reading that document's own editorial description in site/descriptions.json",
		"-- every one marked `origin: \"read\"`, i.e. written by someone reading the text -- together with",
		"its title, kind, pontiff and date off the manifest. NOT from the document texts, and not from",
		"recall. Two exceptions, both closed the same day:",
		"  - `amoris-laetitia` is the one document with no description in any language (the English",
		"    edition is PDF-only, see CLAUDE.md). Its tags are read off the chapter outline in",
		"    `exhortation.amoris-laetitia.it/structure.json`.",
		"  - The first pass read descriptions truncated to 400 characters and 177 of the 271 run longer.",
		"    All 177 were re-read in full and 41 gained a tag the window had cut off (45 tags in all).",
		"    41 in 272 is the measured cost of reading a summary short; the window is closed.",
		"",
		"A slug here that names no document in the build is a FAILED sync, not a warning: it is the",
		"residue of a renamed work, and the tags it holds are lost silently otherwise."
	],
